<lx-callout tone="warn" title="On dev, not released">
This work is on the <code>dev</code> branch. The work is not on <code>main</code>. The work is not a release. <code>main</code> stays at commit <a href="https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/commit/698c9d51dd2228686ffc1bcbf8beb644a3d2b0f4">698c9d5</a> (2026-11-06).
</lx-callout>

This receipt records the desktop app and the web UI that Felix ([@Klix927](https://github.com/Klix927)) added to klanker between 2026-11-10 and 2026-11-18 (Europe/Berlin).

The shared UI lives in `web/`. The desktop app wraps that UI in a Tauri 2 shell under `src-tauri/`. The same UI is a PWA that `klanker serve` can serve.

## What landed

Felix added a Tauri 2 desktop app. The crate name is `klanker_desktop` in `src-tauri/`. The product name is Klanker. The identifier is `org.lolaplex.klanker`. Root scripts in `package.json` start and build the app: `pnpm desktop:dev` and `pnpm desktop:build`.

[PR #44](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/44) (2026-11-11) put the React UI in `web/` and served it as a PWA. `klanker serve` sets `AGENTS_RELAY_WEB_DIR` to vendored files in `src/klanker/_web` when that variable is unset. `scripts/vendor-web.py` copies `web/dist` into that folder. The Docker image builds `web/` in a Node stage and copies the result into the Python image. The runtime image has no Node.

Commit [1b03968](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/commit/1b03968f78b3b2d6f74afe7eb0853bbcdeee3bf1) (2026-11-12) first added `src-tauri/` to this repository.

[PR #48](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/48) (2026-11-18) replaced that first manager with a thin shell. The Rust side now owns only native work:

- one managed local `klanker serve` on `127.0.0.1:8787` (the app adopts a serve that already runs; it does not kill a foreign serve)
- OS keyring for secrets
- tray, close-to-tray, and an Alt+Space raise
- `uv` install and upgrade of the `klanker` CLI (`src-tauri/src/provision.rs`, uv 0.9.16)
- a durable instance registry at `~/.klanker/instances/<id>/instance.json`
- Tailscale peer discovery (`src-tauri/src/discovery.rs`)

The dashboard talks to `klanker serve` over HTTP with a Bearer token. The app stores the token in the OS keyring. The webview does not keep the secret in localStorage.

Later PRs on 2026-11-18 extended that shell: window model ([#52](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/52)), dialogs and legacy import ([#53](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/53)), registry cards ([#62](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/62)), Tailscale discovery ([#63](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/63)), remote mount through the relay ([#64](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/64)), registry reconcile with `remotes.json` ([#73](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/73)), keyring by endpoint host ([#71](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/71)), re-auth ([#72](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/72)), real restart ([#74](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/74)), and presence offers in the add-instance modal ([#75](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/75)).

Instance kinds in `web/src/types/klanker.ts` are `local` and `remote` only.

## Web and PWA polish

Felix also improved the phone and browser surface. Chat replies render as Markdown. Messages and code blocks have a copy control. Touch targets are at least 44px. The composer uses a 16px font on small screens so iOS Safari does not zoom the page. Further commits fix the iOS PWA viewport, keyboard overlap, and safe-area layout.

The Markdown chat work landed on `dev` as commit [09c6eaf](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/commit/09c6eaf) (2026-11-14), which cites PR #47. GitHub shows that pull request as closed, not merged. The zoom fix from the closed PR #46 is in later commits, including [PR #49](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/49).

## Other notable work in the same window

Between 2026-11-10 and 2026-11-12 Felix also landed the workspace and persona CLI (PRs [#26](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/26) through [#41](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/41)): `klanker workspace create|list`, `klanker persona list|add|inbox|task|handoff`, and a stricter host layout. `klanker serve` now refuses a legacy host layout until the operator runs `agents-workspace migrate`.

A later commit, [8eb756b](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/commit/8eb756b), moved `agents-keys`, `agents-voice`, `agents-store`, and `agents-browser` to core dependencies and added the `mcp.browser.read-url` module.

