## How to build and run

These commands come from `package.json`, `src-tauri/tauri.conf.json`, `scripts/vendor-web.py`, and `src/klanker/web_assets.py`. This receipt does not re-run them.

Install the root package dependencies:

```bash
pnpm install
```

Start the desktop app in development mode. This command starts the `web/` dev server on port 1420 and then starts the Tauri shell:

```bash
pnpm desktop:dev
```

Build the desktop app:

```bash
pnpm desktop:build
```

Build the web UI only:

```bash
pnpm --dir web install
pnpm --dir web build
```

Vendor the web build into the Python package, then start the serve. Set `RELAY_WEB_TOKEN` first:

```bash
python scripts/vendor-web.py
klanker serve
```

A managed desktop serve uses `~/.klanker/instances/default` as `AGENTS_HOST_DIR`. The first start can also install the CLI with `uv tool install klanker` from the Settings panel.

## Known gaps and next steps

- The desktop app does not provision Docker, VPS, or NAS instances yet. Instance kinds are `local` and `remote` only.
- A managed local serve uses `~/.klanker/instances/default` as the host root. A CLI `klanker serve` uses `~/.agents` by default. These are two different host roots.
- The shared `client-repl`, `client-overlay`, and `client-host` layers are not in this repository. The CLI REPL stays in `src/klanker/shell/`. The GUI is the `web/` UI in a Tauri webview.
- There is no CI job that builds `web/` or the Tauri app. Felix's PRs targeted `dev`, so they did not get a passing pytest job on GitHub Actions.
- The updater public key in `src-tauri/tauri.conf.json` is still the placeholder `REPLACE_WITH_KLANKER_MINISIGN_PUBKEY`.
- `.github/workflows/publish.yml` publishes the Python package only. That workflow does not vendor `web/` and does not ship desktop artifacts or `latest.json`.
- `agents-store>=0.0.1` is a new core dependency. That package is not on PyPI (HTTP 404 on 2026-11-19).
- `README.md` still lists "Desktop Companion GUI" as an unchecked roadmap item. The README does not document `pnpm desktop:dev` or `web/`.
- The private repo `Lolaplex/klanker-desktop` still exists and still holds the older Rust manager. This repo does not vendor that tree as-is.
- Open PR [#22](https://github.com/Lolaplex/klanker/pull/22) (receipt-read guards) is not part of this desktop work. That PR is not ready to merge.

